  "narrative": {
    "top_frame": "Tenth-inning baseball is not usually where you find your answers, but Kansas City left one open and Andujar walked through it.",
    "what_this_means": "This team doesn't fold when the game is tied. They had their moment in the fifth. Scraped together two runs and took the lead. And then watched it slip in the eighth. The bullpen fractured late. Kyle Hart gave back three in less than an inning, and suddenly they were chasing again in the tenth. This is where the fragility lives. Not in the losing. In the fact that they need perfect conditions to hold a one-run game. They scored three runs in the tenth to retake the lead, and it still wasn't enough. Andujar had two hits that moved runners, but the real cost was the inning Hart couldn't survive. You don't lose games like this by accident. They had the game twice. The bullpen didn't protect either lead.",
    "what_to_watch": "Randy Dobnak takes the ball for Kansas City tonight at 1:10. His 1.86 ERA is a reminder that Canning walks into a matchup where the margin for error is already thin.",
